From: Fedora audiofile maintainers
Date: Wed, 3 Feb 2016 21:21:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid undefined negative left shifts

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later AND BSD-3-Clause
Upstream-Status: Downstream [production hunk accepted as b62c902dd258125cac86cd2df21fc898035a43d3]
Origin: https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/audiofile/raw/rawhide/f/audiofile-0.3.6-left-shift-neg.patch

Use an unsigned shift before subtraction so GCC 14 can evaluate the signed
minimum constants without invoking undefined behavior. The production fix
was accepted upstream; Fedora carries the same correction in the three
test-only constants.

---
 libaudiofile/modules/SimpleModule.h | 2 +-
 test/FloatToInt.cpp                 | 2 +-
 test/IntToFloat.cpp                 | 2 +-
 test/Sign.cpp                       | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/libaudiofile/modules/SimpleModule.h
+++ b/libaudiofile/modules/SimpleModule.h
@@ -126 +126 @@
-	static const int kMinSignedValue = -1 << kScaleBits;
+	static const int kMinSignedValue = 0 - (1U << kScaleBits);
--- a/test/FloatToInt.cpp
+++ b/test/FloatToInt.cpp
@@ -118 +118 @@
-static const int32_t kMinInt24 = -1<<23;
+static const int32_t kMinInt24 = 0 - (1U << 23);
--- a/test/IntToFloat.cpp
+++ b/test/IntToFloat.cpp
@@ -120 +120 @@
-static const int32_t kMinInt24 = -1<<23;
+static const int32_t kMinInt24 = 0 - (1U << 23);
--- a/test/Sign.cpp
+++ b/test/Sign.cpp
@@ -119 +119 @@
-static const int32_t kMinInt24 = -1<<23;
+static const int32_t kMinInt24 = 0 - (1U << 23);
